{
  "schema_version": 3,
  "id": "2026-09-17-background-run-project-identity",
  "problem_type": "Submitted background generation re-reads the current project",
  "symptom": "A generation, recovery or relay submitted in project A and finished after the user switched to B localized its result, took its task project, extracted relay frames or wrote progress and results against B (or dropped them) instead of A",
  "direct_cause": "catalogTaskActions and recoverTaskActions localized results with getActiveWorkbenchProjectId after polling; taskApi overwrote extras.projectId with getDesktopActiveProjectId at submit, stream and poll; relayFrameResolver, video depth and shot verify read the current project; main runTask/taskResultQuery fell back to activeTaskProjectFallback (the committed GUI project) and a poll could re-adopt a project for a cached task",
  "class_root": "A run's project identity was never an attribute of the run: every step asked 'which project is open now' instead of reading the identity fixed when the paid task was submitted, so identity drifted with UI navigation",
  "affected_population": [
    "Single node generation, variants and in-place regenerate",
    "Batch and dependency-wave generation",
    "Streaming text generation",
    "Timeout recovery (free re-poll), including after restart",
    "Video relay first-frame extraction",
    "Local video depth derivation",
    "Shot verify after batch completion",
    "ComfyUI candidate test, prompt refine, browser prompt extraction task submissions",
    "Main-process task submit and poll localization, diagnostics bundle and agent trace project"
  ],
  "scope_paths": [
    "electron/catalog/customCallDispatch.ts",
    "electron/diagnostics/agentTraceIpc.ts",
    "electron/diagnostics/diagnosticsIpc.ts",
    "electron/tasks/",
    "electron/runtime.ts",
