  ],
  "external_sources": [],
  "internal_only_reason": "Approved behavior §2 rule 3 (submitted background generation belongs to the original project) and Nomi's own run records, task cache and per-project persistence define the invariant; no third-party API is involved.",
  "invariants": [
    "A run's project identity (full ProjectBinding) is fixed at submission, persisted on the run record (GenerationNodeRunRecord.projectId) and is the only source of truth for that run",
    "Polling and recovery repeat the task's own identity; nothing re-reads the current project",
    "An outcome lands in the original project: the store while that exact binding is open, otherwise the project's own disk copy through localProjectStore; the newly open project has zero side effects",
    "taskApi never fills or overrides a task project; the identity is an explicit argument (null = explicitly no project) and a request that names a different project is refused",
    "Main never supplies a task project from the committed GUI project; a poll naming a different project than the cached task is refused (TASK_PROJECT_MISMATCH)",
    "Old run records without projectId derive it from the project the record is persisted in; a record naming another project is refused with an explanation"
  ],
